(CCRS FILE PROCESSING FRAMEWORK USER GUIDE) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(PURPOSE) Tj
0 -14 Td
(This application is an internal team tool that helps staff work with CCRS files more ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(efficiently. Today it supports referral JSON processing, value updates, output ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(packaging, and optional upload workflows, and it is designed to expand over time to ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(support additional CCRS file types and internal use cases.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(WHAT THE APP CAN DO) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Read any source file that ends with `.json`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Generate new referral JSON files without needing a source folder) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Save processed JSON files using a user-chosen output name) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Create one `.gz` file using a user-chosen archive name) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Update referral-related JSON values) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Show live previews for `Referral Number`, `Station ID`, `Payment Authority Code`, ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(output JSON names, and the final `.gz` name) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Keep or remove processed JSON files after the `.gz` file is created) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Optionally upload the `.gz` file to `DEV`, `PPD`, or `SQA`) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(BEFORE YOU START) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Make sure you have:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- a source folder containing CCRS `.json` files for the workflow you are running) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- an output folder where processed files should be saved) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- a valid `WinSCP.ini` file or a ready-to-use `config\\upload_credentials.json` file if ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(you plan to use upload) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(HOW TO RUN THE APP) Tj
0 -14 Td
(This guide assumes users are running the packaged Windows application.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(To start the app:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- open the folder that contains `CCRS File Processing Framework.exe`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- double-click `CCRS File Processing Framework.exe`) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(On first run, the app creates local folders next to the `.exe`, including:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `config`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `logs`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `upload_import`) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Users should update the files in that generated `config` folder next to the `.exe`, not ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(the source-code folder.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(MAIN WORKFLOW) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The main `Referral Files` area now has two sub-tabs:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `Edit Existing Files` for updating existing JSON files from a source folder) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `Generate New Files` for creating new referral JSON files from scratch) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. CHOOSE SOURCE FOLDER) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Use the `Source` section to choose the folder that contains the input `.json` files.) Tj
ET
endstream
